      "id": "c1",
      "type": "comment",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 30,
      "fields": {
        "text": "The ComfyUI regional-prompting / masked-inpaint pattern: repaint one region at a time, each pass protected by its own mask, so finished regions are never re-rolled by the next pass. Every pass uses Nano Banana Edit, which the editor's own mask verification (proof/inpaint-mask-verification.md in the nanoodle repo) measured honouring a mask: the masked region changes, pixels outside stay put. Masks are white = repaint, black = keep, at the photo's full size. In the editor you can delete a Mask input and brush the mask straight onto its Inpaint node instead. See recipes/regional-inpaint-passes.md."
      },
      "w": 860,
      "name": "Regional inpaint passes - three masks, three repaints, nothing else moves"
    },
